 "summary": "Brian Reid's document specification language and compiler (CMU, 1976-80, later sold by Unilogic): authors mark up text with @-commands naming logical environments (@section, @begin(quotation)...@end(quotation)) while separately written document-format definitions decide presentation. It pioneered the separation of content and style later taken up by GML/SGML, LaTeX and Scribble.",
